    <string name="guide_eyebrow">CREATIVE FLOW</string>
    <string name="guide_title">Make tracing feel smoother.</string>
    <string name="guide_subtitle">A fast setup guide for cleaner references, better placement, and less fighting with the overlay.</string>
    <string name="guide_hero_title">Best workflow</string>
    <string name="guide_hero_body">Choose a reference, fit it loosely, lower opacity, switch on a guide, then use Draw Mode before drawing in your art app.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_one">1. Start with opacity around 55 percent so your drawing strokes stay visible over the reference.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_two">2. Use Grayscale or Line Boost when the image is colorful or low contrast.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_three">3. Use Grid, Thirds, or Diagonal guides for faces, poses, symmetry, and composition checks.</string>
    <string name="guide_step_four">4. Tap Draw Mode when placement is finished. The overlay becomes touch-through so your drawing app receives the pen or finger input.</string>
